claim.claim-text:
2. The dialysis treatment device of claim 1, wherein
the monitoring system is configured to confirm presence of a helper at the first location, the helper being different from the patient receiving treatment by the medical treatment component;
the monitoring system being further configured to
automatically and at predefined time intervals during the treatment session, generate one or more verification request signals requesting the helper to manually input of a verification response into a user interface of the monitoring system in response to the one or more verification request signals, the verification response verifying that the helper is present at the first location, and identifying that the helper is an authorized helper to be at the first location;
the monitoring system being further configured to confirm a pattern of presences of the helper over a plurality of said predefined time intervals during of said treatment session in which said medical treatment component is operative to deliver therapy to the patient based on said verifying and identifying; and
the monitoring system generating a signal indicative of an abnormal condition when the pattern of presences of the authorized helper is not confirmed and causing the medical treatment component to go into a failsafe operational mode to reduce risks to the patient during said treatment session.

8. A method for controlling an extracorporeal blood treatment machine at a first location to reduce risk of continuing blood treatment of a patient in the absence of an authorized helper other than the patient received the blood treatment in an immediate vicinity of the extracorporeal blood treatment machine, comprising:
providing the extracorporeal blood treatment machine at the first location, the extracorporeal blood treatment machine having controller connected to a network or the Internet and communicating with information servers and/or remote terminals at a second location remote from the first location;
obtaining instructions by the controller from the servers, the instructions including at least prescription information specific to the patient at the first location;
reporting status and/or notifying of conditions of the extracorporeal blood treatment machine by the controller to the information servers and/or remote terminals at the second location; and
receiving at a user interface of the extracorporeal treatment machine instructions from an operator to control medical treatment functions of the extracorporeal machine.
